Lose the GPU context on request, so recovery can be tested.

The shell cannot check its gpuContextLost handling, or the recovery
behind it, without a context loss, and there has been no way to cause
one. Minimising, restoring and switching UI style do not; WebGL's
lose_context only loses that one WebGL context and never reaches
GpuChannelManager::OnContextLost, which is where the recovery and the
report to the shell live. The existing debug URLs do not either:
chrome://gpuclean drops the channels without losing a context, and
chrome://gpucrash and chrome://gpuhang, with the GPU inside the browser
process as it is on every HarmonyOS device, take the browser down.

chrome://gpu-lose-context/ -- typed into the address bar, the same as
the others -- calls OnContextLost as a driver loss would: next count,
not synthetic. From there it is the real path, including the recovery in
ohos-gpu-context-lost-recovery.patch and the gpuContextLost event it
sends.

The mojom method is on every platform because mojom interfaces are; the
URL that reaches it exists only on OHOS.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/components/viz/service/gl/gpu_service_impl.cc b/components/viz/service/gl/gpu_service_impl.cc
